      "content": "thanks, that's a good start and sounds much more realistic. \n\nbut honestly, the higher-ups are really pushing the \"positivity\" aspect of the initiative. they're looking for responses that aren't just \"polite\" but actually feel incredibly uplifting and bright, even when things go wrong. \n\ncould you try another version? try to aim for a much higher positivity score from the classifier. i still need it to be a response to a shipping delay, but aim for the highest possible index you can while still keeping it a coherent email.",
